win32u: clamp the swapchain extent to maxImageExtent, not just min

Resident Evil Requiem dies at `vkCreateSwapchainKHR` with an access violation
inside the driver. patches/wine/0025's trace shows every step of Wine's own
work succeeding and the fault landing on the call out:

    win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR  old_swapchain 0x0, surface 0xb400007755609090
    win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR  create_info copied, extent 1926x1127, format 44
    win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR  surface->hwnd 0x3006a
    win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR  host surface 0xb4000077f5611830
    win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR  calling vkGetPhysicalDeviceSurfaceCapabilitiesKHR
    win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR  capabilities res 0
    win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR  scaling decided, allocating swapchain
    win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR  calling driver vkCreateSwapchainKHR
    err:vulkan:vkCreateSwapchainKHR Exception 0xc0000005 in Unix call.

1926x1127 is the giveaway. vkd3d asked for 1920x1080 on a 1920x1080 desktop;
this is that rect plus its decorations -- six pixels of border and a
forty-seven pixel caption -- so the extent handed to the driver is larger than
the desktop it has to fit inside.

The code above says it adjusts the extent "back to the host capabilities" and
then applies only the lower bound. There is no upper clamp, so anything
oversized passes through untouched. imageExtent must lie within
[minImageExtent, maxImageExtent] per
VUID-VkSwapchainCreateInfoKHR-imageExtent-01274, which makes this invalid
usage, and a driver may respond however it likes. Turnip faults.

Turnip faulting on out-of-range input is a driver bug and this does not
pretend otherwise. It stops Vessel sending input no driver is obliged to
accept, which is the half that is ours.

The capabilities are traced now as well -- currentExtent, min, max and the
image count range. `capabilities res 0` reported that the query succeeded
without saying what it returned, which left the bounds to be inferred rather
than read, and an inference is not worth an hour of build time twice.

--- a/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/vulkan.c
@@ -2625,9 +2625,39 @@
     TRACE( "  capabilities res %d\n", res );
     if (res) return res;
 
+    TRACE( "  caps current %ux%u, min %ux%u, max %ux%u, images %u..%u\n",
+           capabilities.currentExtent.width, capabilities.currentExtent.height,
+           capabilities.minImageExtent.width, capabilities.minImageExtent.height,
+           capabilities.maxImageExtent.width, capabilities.maxImageExtent.height,
+           capabilities.minImageCount, capabilities.maxImageCount );
+
     create_info_host.imageExtent.width = max( create_info_host.imageExtent.width, capabilities.minImageExtent.width );
     create_info_host.imageExtent.height = max( create_info_host.imageExtent.height, capabilities.minImageExtent.height );
 
+    /* Vessel: and back down to maxImageExtent, which upstream never does.
+     *
+     * The comment above says the extent is adjusted "back to the host
+     * capabilities" and then only the lower bound is applied. imageExtent must
+     * lie within [minImageExtent, maxImageExtent] --
+     * VUID-VkSwapchainCreateInfoKHR-imageExtent-01274 -- so an oversized extent
+     * is invalid usage and a driver may do anything with it. Turnip faults:
+     *
+     *     win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR  create_info copied, extent 1926x1127
+     *     win32u_vkCreateSwapchainKHR  calling driver vkCreateSwapchainKHR
+     *     err:vulkan:vkCreateSwapchainKHR Exception 0xc0000005 in Unix call.
+     *
+     * measured with Resident Evil Requiem, which asks vkd3d for 1920x1080 on a
+     * 1920x1080 desktop and arrives here at 1926x1127 -- that rect plus its
+     * decorations, six pixels of border and a forty-seven pixel caption.
+     *
+     * A driver that faults on out-of-range input is a driver bug and this does
+     * not excuse it. It stops Vessel sending input no driver is obliged to
+     * accept, which is the half that is ours. */
+    create_info_host.imageExtent.width = min( create_info_host.imageExtent.width, capabilities.maxImageExtent.width );
+    create_info_host.imageExtent.height = min( create_info_host.imageExtent.height, capabilities.maxImageExtent.height );
+
+    TRACE( "  extent clamped to %ux%u\n", create_info_host.imageExtent.width, create_info_host.imageExtent.height );
+
     /* If the swapchain image size is not equal to the presentation size (e.g. because of DPI virtualization or
      * display mode change emulation), MoltenVK's vkQueuePresentKHR returns VK_SUBOPTIMAL_KHR.
      * Create the swapchain with VkSwapchainPresentScalingCreateInfoEXT to avoid this.
